WEBVTT


00:02:11.673 --> 00:02:14.051
Yeah, Walter. Hi, it's George.


00:02:14.134 --> 00:02:16.887
I know it's my third call on a Saturday,


00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:20.975
but I'm having a bit of a problem
with the Lockwise Helping Hand account.


00:02:21.058 --> 00:02:24.278
Now, I know it's your baby,
and I know you'll straighten it out,


00:02:24.353 --> 00:02:28.654
but, well, I'm thinking of heading into
the office today to see if I can sort it out.


00:02:28.732 --> 00:02:31.986
So, no problems. We'll see you on Monday.


00:02:32.069 --> 00:02:35.949
Don't worry about it.
Give my love to Rebecca. Bye-bye.


00:02:38.116 --> 00:02:40.289
- Barbara, stop it.
- No.


00:02:40.369 --> 00:02:42.542
- You need this.
- No, I will not.


00:02:42.871 --> 00:02:43.997
George!


00:02:44.081 --> 00:02:45.924
George, yes. Where is George?


00:02:46.041 --> 00:02:48.043
- I would like to speak to him.
- I don't know.


00:02:48.126 --> 00:02:50.595
I don't even know who you are, young lady.


00:02:51.713 --> 00:02:53.215
- George.
- Thank God.


00:02:53.298 --> 00:02:55.721
George, who is this young lady?


00:02:56.385 --> 00:02:58.103
- Here, honey.
- That's...


00:02:58.220 --> 00:02:59.972
I can't do this.


00:03:00.055 --> 00:03:01.602
That's my wife, Mom.


00:03:01.723 --> 00:03:04.476
No. She's too young.


00:03:04.601 --> 00:03:06.274
How old is she?


00:03:06.395 --> 00:03:08.022
We were married nine years ago, remember?


00:03:08.105 --> 00:03:09.732
She's nine years old?


00:03:09.815 --> 00:03:13.319
Our marriage is nine years old,
our marriage.


00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:19.749
She's the second one.


00:03:20.784 --> 00:03:23.537
No. I adored the other one.


00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:26.419
I know, Mom, but,
you know, she tried to kill me.


00:03:26.498 --> 00:03:28.967
No, she didn't.
That was just a little hit-and-run.


00:03:29.084 --> 00:03:31.758
Yeah, well, I was in traction for two months.


00:03:31.837 --> 00:03:33.760
I don't remember that.


00:03:35.257 --> 00:03:37.635
- Here you go.
- I like this one.


00:03:37.759 --> 00:03:40.603
- Well, that's the most popular one.
- Yeah.


00:03:40.971 --> 00:03:42.473
There you go.


00:03:46.685 --> 00:03:49.484
- We aren't done with this.
- Yes, I know. I know.


00:03:49.604 --> 00:03:52.232
And why are you wearing a shirt and tie
on a Saturday?


00:03:52.315 --> 00:03:54.113
I have to go into the office.


00:03:54.234 --> 00:03:56.282
- You're going into the office?
- Yes.


00:03:56.403 --> 00:03:58.030
- When?
- Now.


00:03:58.113 --> 00:04:01.117
George, aren't you forgetting something?


00:04:02.159 --> 00:04:04.127
No, I'm not.


00:04:05.078 --> 00:04:06.455
I love you.


00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:09.629
Nice try. Your son.


00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:13.254
You promised him you would take him
to his baseball game today.


00:04:13.336 --> 00:04:16.340
I'm not telling him this time. You do it.


00:04:16.465 --> 00:04:21.016
Honey, I'll be back in time.
The game doesn't start until 2:00.


00:04:21.136 --> 00:04:22.137
1100.


00:04:22.763 --> 00:04:24.436
I'll be back.


00:04:24.598 --> 00:04:27.818
Mom, Dad, Grandma isn't eating.


00:04:29.311 --> 00:04:32.485
God, I hate old people.


00:04:32.481 --> 00:04:34.324
Watch your mouth, young lady.


00:04:34.441 --> 00:04:37.285
Why? It's not like she understands
anything we're saying.


00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:40.034
You know what? I've had
just about enough of your attitude.


00:04:41.156 --> 00:04:43.204
Hello? You listening?


00:04:43.492 --> 00:04:47.167
iPod. They were made
to ignore the stepmother.


00:04:47.287 --> 00:04:48.254
George?


00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:51.334
Honey, would you take those things off,
please, and listen to your mother?


00:04:52.292 --> 00:04:54.670
Okay, she is not my mother.


00:04:55.212 --> 00:04:57.010
She's the mother of that thing.


00:04:57.172 --> 00:04:58.890
- You're the thing.
- You're a thing.


00:04:59.007 --> 00:05:01.635
- You're a thing, sister.
- Don't call me that.


00:05:02.219 --> 00:05:05.689
Dad, I'm really excited
about the game today.


00:05:05.806 --> 00:05:08.150
It's gonna be so cool having you there.


00:05:08.850 --> 00:05:12.855
Jeremy's dad is always there,
but he yells at me if I miss the ball.


00:05:12.979 --> 00:05:14.981
Well, that's not gonna happen today, son.


00:05:15.065 --> 00:05:16.692
Now, I've got to run to the office,


00:05:16.817 --> 00:05:19.366
but I'll be back in time
to take you to your game.


00:05:19.444 --> 00:05:20.787
You promise?


00:05:21.863 --> 00:05:23.706
Scout's honor.


00:05:28.787 --> 00:05:29.788
Don't forget. 1:00.


00:05:29.871 --> 00:05:30.963
He's not coming.


00:05:31.790 --> 00:05:34.213
<i>That was the Star Trek sign.</i>


00:05:34.292 --> 00:05:35.885
He's a Trekkie.


00:05:36.378 --> 00:05:37.880
And so am I.


00:06:05.866 --> 00:06:07.743
- Morning, Jackie.
- Hello.


00:06:07.826 --> 00:06:10.249
Don't you wish it was this quiet every day?


00:06:10.328 --> 00:06:12.547
Be careful what you wish for.


00:06:25.927 --> 00:06:28.897
<i>Gotta be mine</i>


00:06:33.018 --> 00:06:35.567
<i>Gotta be strong</i>


00:06:35.937 --> 00:06:38.736
<i>A little While</i>


00:06:38.857 --> 00:06:42.532
<i>And you got nothing to be guilty of</i>


00:06:42.611 --> 00:06:44.534
<i>You might not wanna sing that song.</i>


00:06:53.705 --> 00:06:55.048
Okay. Shred everything.


00:06:55.332 --> 00:06:57.334
My shredder's broken.
I need another shredder!


00:06:57.417 --> 00:06:58.794
- Here we go!
- Who's got one?


00:06:58.877 --> 00:07:00.129
Don't leave any evidence. Nothing. Okay?


00:07:00.211 --> 00:07:01.884
- Put 'em in a box!
- Let me through. Let me through.


00:07:01.963 --> 00:07:04.807
Shred everything! Here, here. Right here!


00:07:08.678 --> 00:07:09.930
All the boxes!


00:07:12.182 --> 00:07:14.435
All right. Grab those two!
What are you doing?


00:07:15.685 --> 00:07:17.437
Just get it in here! Anything!


00:07:20.231 --> 00:07:21.653
I got one more!


00:07:21.733 --> 00:07:23.576
- Is it the last quarter?
- Yeah.


00:07:25.904 --> 00:07:26.996
Dump everything!


00:07:29.074 --> 00:07:30.166
George, come in here, buddy.


00:07:31.618 --> 00:07:32.961
Come in, come in, come in.


00:07:33.078 --> 00:07:34.830
Walter, what's going on?


00:07:34.913 --> 00:07:36.836
Hey, listen, pull your money out of the bank,


00:07:36.915 --> 00:07:39.589
cash in all your stocks and bonds
by 10:00 a.m. Monday morning.


00:07:40.085 --> 00:07:41.132
Why?


00:07:41.544 --> 00:07:44.718
Well, CNN is doing
one of those investigative reports


00:07:44.798 --> 00:07:46.516
about Lockwise Industries.


00:07:48.343 --> 00:07:50.846
That's fantastic.
That'll be great for business.


00:07:50.971 --> 00:07:54.817
Not really. They're gonna say we've been
running a Ponzi scheme for seven years.


00:07:56.476 --> 00:07:59.525
Well, they can't say that, Walter.
That's libelous.


00:07:59.646 --> 00:08:03.367
I mean, this firm's been operating
successfully for over 100 years.


00:08:03.483 --> 00:08:07.158
Yeah, yeah, they're focusing
on the charity division, Helping Hands.


00:08:07.237 --> 00:08:10.286
Helping Hands has been going strong
for over eight years.


00:08:10.365 --> 00:08:11.708
I should know. I'm CFO.


00:08:12.867 --> 00:08:14.039
Yeah. Yeah, you are.


00:08:14.119 --> 00:08:16.417
Could you say that again,
the part about the CFO?


00:08:17.247 --> 00:08:19.545
I'm CFO. I should know.


00:08:19.958 --> 00:08:21.835
Right. Perfect, perfect. Thanks.


00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:26.682
Walter, are they reporting
that it's our division?


00:08:27.048 --> 00:08:28.516
Yeah. Your division.


00:08:28.967 --> 00:08:30.514
But I have all the records.


00:08:31.094 --> 00:08:32.937
Say that again.


00:08:33.847 --> 00:08:35.975
But I have all the records.


00:08:36.141 --> 00:08:38.018
Perfect. Now shred them.


00:08:38.518 --> 00:08:39.895
- Walter.
- Yeah.


00:08:40.645 --> 00:08:41.942
What are you saying?


00:08:42.313 --> 00:08:43.986
I'm saying that all the monies


00:08:44.065 --> 00:08:48.912
that came into Lockwise Industries'
Helping Hands charity investment group


00:08:48.987 --> 00:08:51.206
are part of a big, old Ponzi scheme.


00:08:52.198 --> 00:08:53.324
What?


00:08:53.992 --> 00:08:55.289
Yeah. Christ.


00:08:55.368 --> 00:08:57.837
It worked for a while.


00:08:58.204 --> 00:09:00.798
I almost feel bad for hanging
you out to dry like this.


00:09:00.874 --> 00:09:03.593
You should see your face, dude.


00:09:04.085 --> 00:09:07.464
And by the way,
this is not gonna be pretty for you.


00:09:07.547 --> 00:09:09.549
I feel awful.


00:09:09.632 --> 00:09:10.884
Horrible.


00:09:10.967 --> 00:09:12.514
What? But...


00:09:13.219 --> 00:09:14.266
For me?


00:09:14.345 --> 00:09:16.598
You were a lowly accountant, remember?


00:09:16.681 --> 00:09:20.481
And then I pull you out of bookkeeping
and make you the CFO.


00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:23.689
I mean, you had no experience
whatsoever. None. None at all.


00:09:23.772 --> 00:09:27.493
I had worked here five years
prior to that, Walter.


00:09:27.567 --> 00:09:32.494
- I was working hard. I thought I earned it.
- You did work hard.


00:09:32.614 --> 00:09:36.414
Nobody earns it around here.
I had to bang my way to the top.


00:09:36.493 --> 00:09:39.042
And there's a lot of big women
on the Board of Directors here.


00:09:39.120 --> 00:09:42.169
And that was hard,
and it was hard to stay hard.


00:09:42.248 --> 00:09:44.876
So don't talk to me about "hard."


00:09:45.085 --> 00:09:50.057
Okay? You were paid a seven-figure salary
for exactly this reason.


00:09:50.590 --> 00:09:51.933
What reason?


00:09:52.926 --> 00:09:56.976
So you could take the fall.
Man, you've been paid to be screwed.


00:09:57.055 --> 00:09:59.274
Kind of jealous. Oh, well.


00:09:59.516 --> 00:10:03.271
Walter, I knew nothing about this.


00:10:03.353 --> 00:10:05.731
Yeah, I know. I know. Sorry.


00:10:06.272 --> 00:10:08.525
Would have ruined it if you had, kind of.


00:10:10.443 --> 00:10:14.073
Well, that explains why I couldn't get
those accounts to balance.


00:10:14.155 --> 00:10:15.748
Now you're thinking.


00:10:16.866 --> 00:10:19.995
What about the charities?
Walter, 82 charities.


00:10:20.120 --> 00:10:21.713
They think their monies are safe.


00:10:21.788 --> 00:10:23.916
I'm handing you over to the Feds,


00:10:24.082 --> 00:10:27.837
and all you care about
is the stupid charities?


00:10:29.295 --> 00:10:30.672
By the way, there's only 12 charities.


00:10:31.965 --> 00:10:33.967
There's 82 charities.


00:10:34.425 --> 00:10:38.601
No, there's 12. The other 70 companies
were set up by the Malone family.


00:10:39.973 --> 00:10:41.099
Awkward.


00:10:43.476 --> 00:10:44.773
The Mafia Malones?


00:10:45.019 --> 00:10:47.272
You've been laundering money, dude.


00:10:47.355 --> 00:10:50.108
Yeah, this is gonna be really awful for you.


00:10:51.568 --> 00:10:53.195
Hey, man, be careful
when you start your car.


00:10:56.197 --> 00:10:58.541
This is not happening.


00:10:59.033 --> 00:11:02.537
A Ponzi scheme? A Ponzi scheme?


00:11:03.454 --> 00:11:07.379
Walter, where are the investors' monies?


00:11:09.627 --> 00:11:12.255
Walter? Walter!


00:11:19.804 --> 00:11:25.732
Okay, calm down. Calm, calm, calm.
Calm down.


00:11:25.810 --> 00:11:27.687
That's it. That's it.


00:11:27.770 --> 00:11:30.569
Just calm down.


00:11:31.441 --> 00:11:34.945
I'm not calming. I'm not calming.
I'm not calming.


00:11:50.418 --> 00:11:52.671
<i>- Hey, boss, just the person I wanna see.
- What do you have?</i>


00:11:52.754 --> 00:11:55.348
So I've been looking
into the Malone crime family, right?


00:11:55.423 --> 00:11:56.424
And the more I look at them,


00:11:56.549 --> 00:11:58.176
I'm finding that they're connected
to this company


00:11:58.259 --> 00:12:00.682
that does a lot of charity
investment work, called Lockwise.


00:12:00.762 --> 00:12:01.763
Yes?


00:12:01.846 --> 00:12:03.769
I think they may be
laundering money through them.


00:12:03.890 --> 00:12:06.268
- We've been after these guys for years.
- Yeah.


00:12:06.351 --> 00:12:08.445
Why don't you see
what you can find out, okay?


00:12:08.519 --> 00:12:09.862
Okay.


00:12:09.938 --> 00:12:11.440
Thanks a lot.


00:13:13.334 --> 00:13:14.677
George?


00:13:18.589 --> 00:13:21.263
I've been calling you for hours.


00:13:22.760 --> 00:13:25.013
Yeah, I know. I know.


00:13:25.680 --> 00:13:26.727
How is he?


00:13:27.348 --> 00:13:30.352
- He was upset, but he'll be fine.
- That's good.


00:13:30.601 --> 00:13:32.274
Is it true?


00:13:33.229 --> 00:13:34.276
What?


00:13:34.355 --> 00:13:37.199
Come on, George.
Don't play games with me.


00:13:37.275 --> 00:13:39.949
All the wives were talking about it
at the field today.


00:13:41.696 --> 00:13:42.868
Honey.


00:13:43.281 --> 00:13:47.331
I swear I had no idea this was going on.


00:13:47.410 --> 00:13:48.411
Okay? None.


00:13:48.536 --> 00:13:51.506
I walked into the office,
and there's Walter, and he's saying,


00:13:51.581 --> 00:13:54.380
"Why don't you shred stuff?
Shred whatever you have.


00:13:54.459 --> 00:13:56.678
"Shred what's in your desk.
Just shred everything."


00:13:56.753 --> 00:13:58.380
And I'm going, "What's going on?"


00:13:58.463 --> 00:14:00.386
And he's saying,
"You're gonna take the fall for this,


00:14:00.465 --> 00:14:04.515
"because it's a Ponzi scheme.
It's a Ponzi scheme, and you're the one.


00:14:04.594 --> 00:14:07.017
"You're going down,
'cause you're the CFO."


00:14:07.096 --> 00:14:12.068
You know? I mean, they gave
Bernie Madoff 200 years, honey.


00:14:12.143 --> 00:14:15.238
What do you think they're gonna do to me?
What do you think they're gonna do?


00:14:15.396 --> 00:14:18.195
And what's gonna happen with the kids?
What's gonna happen?


00:14:18.274 --> 00:14:20.743
Howie's afraid, you know,
"Dad, you missed a game."


00:14:20.818 --> 00:14:23.116
<i>I'm gonna miss 38 seasons.</i>


00:14:23.237 --> 00:14:25.615
Sweetheart, I'm in trouble.


00:14:26.991 --> 00:14:29.915
- Calm down.
- Okay.


00:14:32.246 --> 00:14:34.248
- We need to get a lawyer.
- A lawyer.


00:14:34.332 --> 00:14:36.630
And then you need to go to your mom's


00:14:36.751 --> 00:14:38.469
and go find your mom's Valium.


00:14:38.586 --> 00:14:40.509
Get a Valium out of my mom's purse.


00:14:40.588 --> 00:14:42.886
- Okay. Can you do that? Like right now.
- Okay.


00:14:42.965 --> 00:14:44.592
And you need to calm down.


00:14:45.259 --> 00:14:46.886
- Honey.
- It's gonna be okay.


00:14:46.969 --> 00:14:48.471
- It will be. It will be.
- Yes.


00:14:48.596 --> 00:14:51.770
You know, minimum security.
It's not that bad.


00:14:52.975 --> 00:14:54.192
Hey, Madea.


00:14:54.644 --> 00:14:57.944
Hey, Lorraine, how you doing?
Good to see you.


00:15:03.111 --> 00:15:05.284
Lord, it's a zoo up in there
on the first of the month.


00:15:14.288 --> 00:15:16.791
Excuse me, ma'am. You wanna take this?
I don't feel like taking it back.


00:15:16.874 --> 00:15:19.252
Thank you so much.
It's crazy up in there. Be careful.


00:15:19.335 --> 00:15:21.463
They ain't taking that EBT card.
They stopped taking that.


00:15:21.546 --> 00:15:23.548
I got to go somewhere else that take that.


00:15:24.006 --> 00:15:27.135
Yeah, I got to go burn up my EBT card.


00:15:33.975 --> 00:15:35.818
Give me your money.


00:15:38.479 --> 00:15:40.948
Give me your money.


00:15:42.275 --> 00:15:44.528
That's a cute little gun you got, boy.
Get out this car.


00:15:44.610 --> 00:15:49.912
Lady, I will stab and shoot you.
Give me your money.


00:15:49.991 --> 00:15:52.164
Son, I'm gonna tell you this one time, okay?


00:15:52.243 --> 00:15:54.792
I want you to get out of this car
and go on about your business.


00:15:54.871 --> 00:15:56.214
Go get you a job.


00:15:56.330 --> 00:15:59.004
You ain't supposed to be stealing
from nobody working as hard as I...


00:15:59.083 --> 00:16:01.256
What the hell you got to come over here
and steal from the poor for?


00:16:01.335 --> 00:16:04.134
Get out the car. This is your warning, son.
Get out the car. Now, go on.


00:16:04.213 --> 00:16:05.886
Then give me your money!


00:16:06.090 --> 00:16:09.219
I worked for years to get my Social Security.
Now, I finally got it.


00:16:09.343 --> 00:16:10.435
I ain't on no fixed income.


00:16:10.511 --> 00:16:12.229
<i>I'm on a broke income,
'cause I'm broke as hell.</i>


00:16:12.346 --> 00:16:13.814
Now, I want you
to get the hell out of this car.


00:16:13.890 --> 00:16:17.394
This is your chance. Get out of the car, son.
Go on, now. Go get you a job.


00:16:17.518 --> 00:16:19.896
I'm gonna ask you one more time,
old woman.


00:16:20.021 --> 00:16:21.364
I'm gonna tell you one more time.


00:16:21.439 --> 00:16:26.036
Look here! Get out of this car.
Go find you a job. Do you understand me?


00:16:26.110 --> 00:16:28.784
They got people all over the world
that is working hard,


00:16:28.863 --> 00:16:31.286
and y'all young thugs gonna come
try to take money from somebody.


00:16:31.365 --> 00:16:33.117
That makes me mad.
Now, you about to make me mad.


00:16:33.201 --> 00:16:35.203
You about to piss me off.
Now, get on out the car, son.


00:16:35.369 --> 00:16:36.916
- I'm gonna count to three.
- Okay.


00:16:37.038 --> 00:16:41.794
One, two, three.


00:16:43.753 --> 00:16:45.130
Four


00:16:46.422 --> 00:16:47.548
Five.


00:16:47.882 --> 00:16:51.352
I thought you was gonna count to three.
Son. Son, son, let me tell you something.


00:16:51.427 --> 00:16:53.304
Get out the car
and go on about your business.


00:16:53.387 --> 00:16:56.766
Now, this is your last chance.
This is your last chance. Now I got to go.


00:16:56.891 --> 00:17:01.397
One more time. One, two...


00:17:01.479 --> 00:17:02.731
Three!


00:17:08.903 --> 00:17:10.120
Let's go this way.


00:17:10.655 --> 00:17:12.828
Put your seat belt on.
You need a car seat?


00:17:13.407 --> 00:17:14.784
Come get my money!


00:17:15.117 --> 00:17:17.620
Trying to take my damn money
that I worked this hard for.


00:17:19.413 --> 00:17:20.585
Lady!


00:17:20.748 --> 00:17:22.295
I don't got insurance, lady!


00:17:23.501 --> 00:17:24.798
Slow down! Slow down!


00:17:24.961 --> 00:17:27.510
You're screaming
straight up like a little biatch!


00:17:27.672 --> 00:17:28.764
I want to go home!


00:17:32.093 --> 00:17:35.313
You want the money? You come get it.
I come get the money.


00:17:35.429 --> 00:17:37.306
- I'm a real thug! I'm a real thug!
